  "scope": "Conditional statements over supplied kinds, support edges, spans, formation demands and arrival rates: late occurrence descends from a realized closure of kinds; acyclic support has a deadline without a supplied rank; when every kind brings in less than its formation demands, a combined potential strictly decreases on every live tick, so renewal ends by an explicit deadline; a support-closed population that is balanced, or that supports an excess kind, has a steady configuration fixed by one tick and so renews forever; and on one execution of the constraint-flow process, endless liveness needs both a realized closure of supporters that outlast the tick and a kind that brings in at least its formation demand. The exact mixed-case condition is not yet proved. No physical identification or ethical appraisal is asserted."
